  "verbalization": "Isoswinholide B is implicated in the regulation of Dr hemagglutinin structural subunit through multiple indirect pathways. The drug targets U-87 MG, a cancer cell line, which in turn is targeted by Nomilin and by (2S)-3',4'-Dihydroxy-6,7-Dimethoxyflavan. These compounds, in turn, target the Dr hemagglutinin structural subunit, suggesting a chain of molecular interactions that may influence the protein's structure or function. Additionally, Isoswinholide B is shown to target another kinase, Mitogen-activated protein kinase kinase kinase 13, which is targeted by Phytolaccoside B, which also targets the same subunit. While the direct interaction between Isoswinholide B and Dr hemagglutinin structural subunit is not explicitly stated, the evidence suggests a potential mechanistic link through downstream targets. The integration of these pathways implies that Isoswinholide B may exert its effects via a cascade of molecular events that ultimately modulate the Dr hemagglutinin structural subunit. The evidence supports a plausible mechanism involving kinase inhibition or protein regulation, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be elucidated.",
